A||N||19||fropuff||What should I do?||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||11-03-2000||05:25 PM||||Hey, I just got done yesterday with my custom sub box (actually stimpy's), and I am a little disappointed.  I built it for the fact that I want bass, and now all I can fit in is an 8".  I was planning on a 10".  I was wondering if I should get an 8", or get two regular speakers to put in it.  I am looking at my Crutchfield magazine with all the expensive prices, and I see some 5 1/4"s.   I'm thinking that I could get a pair of these and put them in.  The face of the box is 16.5"x10" exactly.  Would this work?  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Seanh||11-03-2000||05:45 PM||||I just thought I would let you know. <A HREF="http://www.subbox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.subbox.com</A>  place sell kickpanel enclosures to hold mids without any modification to the interior if you are needing midrange detail. You could play around with the design and try to get a 10" up there, I know it could be done. Even a properly amped 8" will sound good. For somthing like this, I would recommend an Image Dynamics subwoofer.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif"> <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||11-03-2000||05:54 PM||||I know that I want to get a sub sometime in the future.  I have almost NO money at all, so I wouldn't be able to buy an amp for a while.  So, I thought that I could get some good 5 1/4s.  Will these work good?  I think it would turn out pretty good.  Thanks.<p>[This message has been edited by fropuff (edited 11-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||11-03-2000||06:02 PM||||I dont know about that. My mind would have to tell me no. It would definatly add to the sound okay, but it would not do really what it should. Are you reffering to 5.25" full range/coax speakers, Midranges/Component setups, or 5.25" woofers? A component set should always be put in the dash or kickpanels. If you are indeed talking about a component set, then No, I dont think you should do that. If you are talking about woofers, then yeah, you could, it would add some bass, probally not all you want, but it would help. If you are thinking of 5.25 woofers, then I would not do that, I would just get yourself an 8" and throw in there. IMO even an unamped 8" would sound better then a pair of 5.25" woofers. IMO of course, do what ever you can afford, but I think you should put a single sub in there as opposed to two smaller ones. <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif"> <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||11-03-2000||06:04 PM||||I was referring to a regular 5.25" speaker set.  Do you really think an 8" sub without an amp would sound good?  I might go for that if it would work.  Thanks for the help. <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula||11-03-2000||06:14 PM||||I've heard 2 kicker 10" subs ran off a head unit (40Wx4, 12W rms)and for some reason, it "bumped"||||reg||1
Z||000006||william_thorniii||11-03-2000||06:17 PM||||seanh,<P>I didn't think the pictures of "your" install was in your silver car.  The fenders were black...  Also on subox.com there isn't any info on kickpanel enclosures.  Is there something you know that I don't?<P>fropuff,<P>This will sound harsh, but nothing will sound good without an amp.  There is no way that anything that requires airspace will have enough power from a headunit.  The amp is the first step young jedi.  <P>I have a Polk component set (6.5" woofers, .75" tweeters db series) and a Polk db10 woofer.  They barely have enough power from my amp (MTX PRO 75x4).  My sub is mounted in the passenger side foot well.<P>My philosophy is if you buy cheap components, you will eventually spend twice as much because you will end up replacing all of your original pieces.  Just save your money and maybe get part of the amp bought for you for X-mas.  If everyone you know chips in a few $...  Or get a job at Circuit City.  An employee gets EVERYTHING at cost.  It will take you longer to get a good system, but you will appreciate it when you are done and can be proud of what you have.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000007||fropuff||11-03-2000||06:22 PM||||Well, I guess I'm not getting anything now.  I might get some 4x10s for the front, but that's all.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||fropuff||11-03-2000||06:27 PM||||What are some good 4x10s that I could get?  I DON'T have much money.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000009||fropuff||11-03-2000||06:36 PM||||How about if I got some 6x9"s for the front dash?  I've heard some people have put them in their Fieros and liked them.  (Gokart and Fiero56).  Should I try this?  That way, I get a little more bass.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Seanh||11-03-2000||06:54 PM||||Your right, nothing will sound very good without an amp. One 8" would throw out more bass and be more efficent then putting two 5.25" speakers in there. If you want to go the 6x9 route, you may be able to get them in there without removing the dash, depends what brand you buy. The car in the pictures I posted was another one on the <A HREF="http://www.subbox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.subbox.com</A>  site. It is the owners car auctually. It is not mine, althought the I did purchase his setup. If your interested in the kickpanel enclosures, then email him. Or email me and I will give you his phone #, they just moved to a larger building and they will be putting up a new server, then they will have their new website, including the boxes that hold 12"'s behind the seats and the kickpanels boxes.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif"> <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fropuff||11-03-2000||07:07 PM||||Does anyone know what brand of 6x9s I could buy so I don't have to remove the dash.  That would be great if I didn't have to.  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000012||stimpy||11-03-2000||09:10 PM||||I don't know what kind of 6x9 would fit properly and not buzz from improper mounting, but I bought a pair of Pioneer coax 4x10 for $100 that sound great just running off of my head unit.  Highly recommended. Pioneer speakers are, IMO the best balance between price and performance for replacement speakers.||||reg||1
